cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite this software release and the accompanying article."
title: "CGDA: centroid-guided data augmentation for domain adaptation in electronic-nose drift compensation"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of centroid-guided data augmentation (CGDA) for
  electronic-nose drift compensation. Class-level target centroids estimated from
  a small labelled calibration set anchor the interpolation of source samples; the
  same frozen feature extractor supports closed-set recognition, unknown-gas
  rejection and environmental event detection through a cosine prototype distance.
authors:
